  "topic": "Read and write Mim (م) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Mim. Like 'm' in 'moon' or 'mother'. Both lips close together — the humming sound!",
      "title": "Meet Mim!",
      "ar": "م",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Mim"
    },
    {
      "en": "A small circle with a tail — like a little tadpole or a mini spiral going right. Mim looks like a tiny MOON (mim = moon in shape). M for Moon, M for Mim!",
      "title": "How to write Mim"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Mim says “ma”.",
      "title": "Mim with fatha",
      "ar": "مَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Mim says “me”.",
      "title": "Mim with kasra",
      "ar": "مِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Mim says “mo”.",
      "title": "Mim with damma",
      "ar": "مُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Muhammad is a great teacher”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "مُحَمَّدٌ مُعَلِّمٌ عَظِيمٌ",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Muhammadun Mu'allimun 'Azim"
    }
  ],
